[16.490316, "o", "The current memory usage on the node is approximately \u001b[1m5.4 GB\u001b[0m (5,849,784,320 bytes), which is about \u001b[1m19.6%\u001b[0m of the total available memory.                                                  \r\n\r\nThis level of usage seems reasonable and should not cause immediate performance issues. However, to ensure optimal performance and prevent potential future bottlenecks, consider        \r\nmonitoring the following:                                                                                                                                                                \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mMemory Usage Trends\u001b[0m: Use queries like \u001b[1;36;40mrate(container_memory_usage_bytes[5m])\u001b[0m to track how memory usage changes over time.                                                             \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCPU Usage\u001b[0m: Check CPU usage with \u001b[1;36;40mrate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total[5m])\u001b[0m to ensure that CPU is not becoming a limiting factor.                                                     \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mDisk I/O and Network Traffic\u001b[0m: Monitor disk I/O and network traffic to identify any potential bottlenecks.                                                                             \r\n\r\nIf you notice consistent high memory or CPU usage, consider optimizing your applications or scaling up the node resources. Regularly reviewing these metrics will help maintain smooth   \r\noperation of your cluster.                                                                                                                                                               \r\n"]
